**Plasm** — `logical_session_ref` + `program`. Clean read-only plans execute inline. Plans containing mutations or a review gate return a `run_ref` for `plasm_run`; do not echo the program there.

`program` is Python source text, not JSON data. Submit exactly one class derived from Program, with build(self), immutable bindings and an explicit return. This tool description contains the static Python semantic reference; incremental domain declarations arrive through plasm_context. Do not copy declarations, instantiate the class or call build. Imports must be supported by Monty's pure Python profile.

Use only taught e#/m#/r# symbols and exact wire names. Pass catalog method arguments by name; Get also accepts its single identity positionally. The class declares a deferred, typed DAG; @compute methods process materialized values later in bounded Monty. Program-owned Python parse, type and plan rejections return needs_fix with a correction; preserve selection criteria and repair within the same logical session. No other source syntax is accepted and failed Python is never retried as another language.

Inspect coverage and operation outcomes. A failed or cancelled run can have completed writes: inspect evidence before issuing further effects. Extend the existing context for missing capabilities. Never open a new session to repair syntax.

Failure evidence belongs to one execution. A new program may perform reads or writes in the same logical session; it does not resume or roll back an earlier execution. Service diagnostics inform the agent but do not determine effect status.


build: immutable DAG; non-null tuples: nested unpacking. Return rowsets; tuples=results; records=data, not envelopes. Literal-ID for/one-clause comprehensions expand (<=256). A fresh `out=[]` immediately followed by a literal-ID loop whose only statement is `out.append(expr)` collects values/effects in order; expr cannot capture out, and aliases are not mutable. No dynamic loops/while/filtered comprehensions/for-else/statement if/general mutation. Other Python mutation=@compute. Callbacks branch; imports: module/@compute.

Cards: exact signatures; eN/mN/rN/vN session-local/append-only. eN.method=root; row.method=entity row/singleton; = ... optional. Relations: row.rN or rows.flat_map(lambda r: r.rN); never rN(). vN=domain identity/constraints; Literal=choices. Comments=data; groups=methods; constraints=JSON/@profile. Inputs=keywords; producer fields=dependencies.

Rows:
where(predicate), select("f", alias="f", derived=lambda r: expr), order_by("f", descending=False), take(n>=0), distinct("f"), union(other), aggregate(n=agg.count()), group_by("f", n=agg.sum("amount")). agg: count/sum/avg/min/max/first/last; union requires the same column names, joins field types without coercion, and dedups first-wins. Project differing schemas explicitly before union. Predicates: truth/comparison/and/or/not; any/all: complete collections; substring/list/one-column RHS membership. Lazy reads; explicit effects. Verify matches/identities before effects. where filters acquired rows; branches keep types; arithmetic drops constraints. query/search.page_size(n).

eN.get(value) or eN.get(identity=value); compound Get: exact named keys; nullary: no identity. Only declared keywords. Get/take(1): scalar fields, identity; empty extraction fails. Entity rows/captures keep identity/authority. Inferred compute selections can retain unchanged original rows from one entity owner; constructed or modified records are values, not receivers. union retains authority iff both arms share catalog/entity authority; else values. Project output fields, not inputs; partial writes list fields. Projections=records (r.field/r["field"]); dicts=dict[str,T], no key guarantees; embedded rows=arrays; nested records/arrays/args.

flat_map(lambda r: rows_or_effect, max_parents=65536): reads/writes; bound 1..65536 optional. map(lambda r: {"key": expr}, max_parents=N): bound 1..256 required. Depth<=16; occurrences<=65536. Captures/f-strings=dependencies. def f(row): typed/defaulted inputs, locals/captures, branches/early return; fallthrough=None. Callbacks: map/flat_map/where/select/iterate; f(value): once, preserving collections; flat_map None=no output, [effect1, effect2]=ordered effects, no mixed values. Pure predicates/projections. Helpers: self.helper(args); _methods allowed; __methods reserved. Pure helpers=values; Plasm helpers=scoped DAGs. No recursion/escape.

@compute: self.method(...): pure Python on materialized inputs. Inference: query -> rows; proven singleton -> row. Annotations optional. eN=catalog, not type; rows: Row/Value[eN]. select=rows; singleton.field=scalar, retaining nullability. Unused declarations=no nodes; invocations checked. Independent inputs; values lack rN/mN authority. Returns: bool/int/float/str, vN, Row, Value[eN], list[T], set[T], T | U/None; Row.field retains its contract. str|None: guard text is not None before text.split(...). dict/list[dict]: mappings with .get(); set[T]=sets. Monty infers returns/bodies/loops/implicit None. Dicts: key/value types, not keys. vN=annotation, not constructor; check returns before effects. Monty Python; no host IO/self calls. Inputs<=256 complete rows; input/output<=1 MiB; exceptions/budgets fail. JsonValue/Blob=JSON; EntityRef=opaque; Money={"__plasm_money": decimal_string}. Exact: money_add(a,b), money_sub(a,b), money_mul(v,f), money_div(v,f), money_compare(a,b)->-1/0/1; f=int/decimal str, no float; currency mismatch fails.

datetime: import date/datetime/timedelta/timezone in module/compute. Typed dates: compare directly; text via .isoformat(), never slicing. Naive/aware preserved. Relative times: runtime date.today()/datetime.now(), never guesses. Bounds: date.today()-timedelta(days=1), .replace(month=1, day=1); literal dates need input.

Get.iterate(lambda r: effect, until=lambda r: test, max_steps=N) re-reads state; exhaustion fails. Effects in program/parent order; failure stops remaining effects/parents. Unreturned writes run; dependent reads see them. Fanout dedupes identities; excludes existing complete members. Failure: retain completed/unknown receipts and service diagnostics; failed dispatch may have effects. New programs read/write in-session; no resume/rollback. Partial/unknown ≠ absence.

class P(Program):
    def build(self):
        return e1.query().where(lambda r: r.score is not None and r.score > 0).select("title")

Absent: AttributeError; select needs presence; guard nullable receivers.
